   "html_text": "Procedural principles of this kind arguably afford a distinct kind of legal agency—at once limiting and enabling—to those who interact with their prescriptions. Arguably, such principles matter more in the ordinary person’s conception of the rule of law than the formal criteria addressed in the previous section. When people worried that the American detention facility in Guantanamo Bay was a “black hole” so far as legality was concerned, for example, it was precisely the lack of these procedural",
